%I A400595 #11 Oct 12 2026 21:28:17
%S A400595 1,1,2,4,6,11,19,32,55,94
%N A400595 Largest m such that one defective in each of two disjoint m-item sets can always be identified in at most n adaptive tests, each returning the number of defectives in a selected subset.
%H A400595 Fedor Karpelevitch, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.38489">Certified exact bounds for adaptive quantitative group testing with two defectives</a>, arXiv:2609.38489 [math.CO], 2026.
%H A400595 Fedor Karpelevitch, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23006289">Reproduction materials for certified exact bounds in two-defective quantitative group testing</a>, version 1.0.0, 2026.
%F A400595 2^floor(n/2) <= a(n) <= floor(sqrt(3^n)).
%F A400595 a(10) >= 136.
%e A400595 For n=3 a(3) = 4: for sets {a1,...,a4} and {b1,...,b4}, test {a1,a2,b1}. After result 2, test {a1}. After result 0, test {a3,b2}, then {b3} after 0 or {a3,b3} after 1. After result 1, test {a1,b2,b3}, then {a3,b1}, {a2,b2} or {b2} after 0, 1 or 2.
%Y A400595 Cf. A000079, A000225, A000325, A132824, A400594.
%Y A400595 Cf. A400600.
%K A400595 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A400595 0,3
%A A400595 _Fedor Karpelevitch_, Sep 30 2026
